ws-node (1.6.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Define /etc/ws/node.json, recording what the node is deployed as:
    deployment_id, site_name, valid_from, location_source and vertical_datum.
    sr copies deployment_id into every sensor reading
  * Install an example at /usr/share/doc/ws-node/examples/node.json rather than
    shipping the file itself to /etc/ws/, where it would become a conffile
    carrying a placeholder deployment onto every node
  * Document the format in the README

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0100

ws-node (1.5.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Move ws-geoloc to pi-data, where it is installed as pi-geo. A node's
    position is a property of the machine rather than of the WildlifeSystems
    software running on it, so it belongs with the other pi-data utilities
  * Depend on pi-data (>= 0.2.0), which is the first version to ship pi-geo

 -- Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0100

